                <pb facs="0518" n="436" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg436"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1092.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <p>The embassy of Mexico has the honor to ask that the Department of State be
                    pleased, if it sees no objection thereto, to recommend to the authorities
                    concerned that the victuals bought in the United States for the town of Ojinaga,
                    Chihuahua, where Gen. Don Gonzalo Luque is in military command, be allowed to go
                    over the new ford that has been opened between Presidio, Tex., and the said town
                    of Chihuahua, by reason of the present circumstances.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Embassy of
                            Mexico</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1911</hi></date>.
                    </dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
